text:
A helicopter, starting from rest, accelerates straight up from the roof of a hospital. The lifting force does work in raising the helicopter. An $870\ \rm{kg}

$ helicopter rises from rest to a speed of $6.8\ \rm{m/s}

$ in a time of $3.6\ \rm{s}

$. During this time it climbs to a height of $8.9\ \rm{m}

$. What is the average power generated by the lifting force?

Calculate the mean free path of air molecules at a pressure of 7.00 x 10$^{-13}

$ atm and a temperature of 300 K. (This pressure is readily attainable in the laboratory.) Model the air molecules as spheres with a radius of 2.00 x 10$^{-10}

$ m.

Calculate the value of $K_{p}

$ for the equation

$C_{(s)} + CO_{2(g)} \leftrightharpoons 2CO_{(g)}

$

given that at a certain temperature

$C_{(s)} + 2H_{2}O_{(g)} \leftrightharpoons CO_{2(g)} + 2H_{2(g)}

$, $K_{p1} = 3.35

$

$H_{2(g)} + CO_{2(g)} \leftrightharpoons H_{2}O_{(g)} + CO_{(g)}

$, $K_{p2} = 0.665

$

The production of ammonia (NH3) under standard conditions at 25C is represented by the following thermochemical equation. $N2(g) + 3 H2(g) --> 2 NH3(g)

$; H = -91.8 kJ How much heat is released when $1.627\times10^{4}

$ grams of ammonia is produced? kJ

The thermal conductivity of aluminum is twice that of brass. Two rods, one of aluminum and the other of brass, are joined together end to end in excellent thermal contact. They are of equal lengths and radii. The free end of the brass rod is maintained at 0$^{\circ}

$C while the free end of the aluminum rod is kept at 200$^{\circ}

$C.

Under these conditions of steady heat flow, what is the temperature at the joint between the two rods?

How much work is done by a person lifting a $2\ \mathrm{kg}

$ object from the bottom of a well at a constant speed of $2\ \mathrm{m/s}

$ for $5\ \mathrm{s}

$?

HClO is a weak acid (Ka = 4.0 x 10$^{-8}

$) and so the salt NaClO acts as a weak base. What is the pH of a solution that is 0.085 M in NaClO at 25 $^{\circ}

$C?

When 0.949 g of CaO is added to 200.0 mL of 0.500 M HCl(aq), a temperature increase of 389 degrees C is observed. Assume the solution's final volume is 200.0 mL, the density is 1.00 g/mL, and the heat capacity is 4.184 J/gC. What is molar heat of reaction, $\Delta H_{rxn}

$, for the reaction of $CaO(s) + 2H^+(aq) = Ca^{2+}(aq) + H_2O(l)

$ in kJ/mol.

An electron is accelerated by a 7.2 kV potential difference. The charge on an electron is $1.60218 \times10^{-19}

$ C and its mass is $9.10939 \times 10^{-31}

$ kg. How strong a magnetic field must be experienced by the electron if its path is a circle of radius 5.9 cm? Answer in units of T.

Dinitrogen monoxide decomposes into nitrogen and oxygen when heated. The initial rate of the reaction is 0.012 M/s. What is the rate of change of the concentration of $N_{2}O

$ (that is, $\frac{\Delta [N_{2}O]}{ \Delta t}

$)?
